sn11.14:6.1 starts: “‘Therefore the person of intelligence,
sn11.14:6.2 starts: Remembering the Buddha’s Teaching,
sn11.14:6.3 starts: Should be devoted to faith and virtue,
sn11.14:6.4 starts: To confidence and vision of the Dhamma.’”
sn11.18:2.1 starts: “‘These all humbly worship you—
sn11.18:2.2 starts: Those versed in the Triple Veda,
sn11.18:2.3 starts: All the khattiyas reigning on earth,
sn11.18:2.4 starts: The Four Great Kings and the glorious Thirty—
sn11.18:2.5 starts: So who, O Sakka, is that spirit
sn11.18:2.6 starts: To whom you bow in worship?’
sn11.18:5.1 starts: “‘I worship as well, O Matali,
sn11.18:5.2 starts: Those householders making merit,
sn11.18:5.3 starts: The lay followers possessed of virtue
sn11.18:5.4 starts: Who righteously maintain a wife.’
sn11.19:4.1 starts: “‘Those for whom lust and hatred
sn11.19:4.2 starts: And ignorance have been expunged,
sn11.19:4.3 starts: The arahants with taints destroyed:
sn11.19:4.4 starts: These are the ones whom I worship, Matali.
